yond timeout\"\n   458→    expected:\n   459→      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n   460→    traces:\n   461→      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n   462→\n   463→  - name: env_default_lc_all\n   464→    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n   465→    inputs:\n   466→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n   467→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   468→    expected:\n   469→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n   470→    traces:\n   471→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   472→\n   473→  - name: env_override_lc_all\n   474→    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n   475→    inputs:\n   476→      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n   477→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   478→    expected:\n   479→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n   480→    traces:\n   481→      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n   482→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   483→\n   484→  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n   485→    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n   486→    inputs:\n   487→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n   488→      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n   489→    expected:\n   490→      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n   491→    traces:\n   492→      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n   493→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"402cfa1d-2bef-44ce-b198-92d20df4fac4","uuid":"caeddea1-dc16-47f3-b70f-03c2726c388a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/98/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel00.0.yaml","content":"id: test-rel00.0\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel00.0 — build lifecycle, cmd/version, pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils\"\nrelease: rel00.0\n\ntraces:\n  - rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n  - prd011-magefiles R1\n  - prd011-magefiles R2\n  - prd011-magefiles R3\n  - prd011-magefiles R4\n  - rel00.0-uc002-format\n  - prd003-format R1\n  - prd003-format R2\n  - prd003-format R3\n  - rel00.0-uc003-sys\n  - prd002-sys R1\n  - prd002-sys R2\n  - prd002-sys R3\n  - prd002-sys R4\n  - rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n  - prd001-testutils R1\n  - prd001-testutils R2\n  - prd001-testutils R3\n  - prd001-testutils R4\n  - prd001-testutils R5\n\npreconditions:\n  - A git repository with at least one tag matching v[0-9]*.\n  - golangci-lint is installed and on PATH.\n  - mage is installed and on PATH.\n  - configuration.yaml exists at the project root with project.binary_dir set to bin.\n\ntest_cases:\n  # --- uc001-magefiles: build lifecycle and version ---\n\n  - name: build_produces_version_binary\n    description: mage build compiles cmd/version to bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/version exists and is executable\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.4\n\n  - name: version_prints_tag\n    description: bin/version prints the latest version tag and exits 0.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_pattern: \"v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.3\n\n  - name: version_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_v_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version -v produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version -v\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_unknown_flag\n    description: bin/version --bogus prints usage to stderr and exits 2.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --bogus\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 2\n      stdout: \"\"\n      stderr_contains: \"usage\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_dev_build\n    description: A build without ldflags prints \"dev\".\n    inputs:\n      command: \"go build -o /tmp/version-dev ./cmd/version && /tmp/version-dev\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"dev\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n\n  - name: lint_passes\n    description: mage lint runs golangci-lint with no warnings.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage lint\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.2\n\n  - name: clean_removes_bin\n    description: mage clean removes the bin/ directory.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/ does not exist\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  - name: clean_idempotent\n    description: mage clean succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage clean && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  # --- uc002-format: pkg/format output formatting ---\n\n  - name: columns_20_entries_80_width\n    description: Columns distributes 20 filenames into a grid fitting 80 columns.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(entries, 80)\"\n      entries: 20 filenames of varying lengths\n    expected:\n      postcondition: each row fits within 80 characters; column count is maximized\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n      - prd003-format R1.4\n\n  - name: columns_empty_input\n    description: Columns returns nil for empty input.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(nil, 80)\"\n    expected:\n      result: nil\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n\n  - name: pad_right\n    description: PadRight pads a string with trailing spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"abc       \"  (abc + 7 spaces)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: pad_left\n    description: PadLeft pads a string with leading spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadLeft(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"       abc\"  (7 spaces + abc)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: display_width_multibyte\n    description: Column width uses rune count, not byte count, for multi-byte strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"café\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"café      \"  (café is 4 runes, padded to 10)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.3\n\n  - name: file_type_color_all_types\n    description: FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI codes for all eight file types.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(mode) for each file type\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      directory: '\"\\033[34m\"'\n      symlink: '\"\\033[36m\"'\n      executable: '\"\\033[32m\"'\n      block_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      char_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      socket: '\"\\033[35m\"'\n      pipe: '\"\\033[33m\"'\n      regular: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.1\n      - prd003-format R2.4\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled\n    description: Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"\\033[0m\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.2\n\n  - name: color_disabled_suppresses_output\n    description: SetColorEnabled(false) causes FileTypeColor and Reset to return empty strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(os.ModeDir) and format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n    expected:\n      file_type_color: '\"\"'\n      reset: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.6\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled_restores_auto\n    description: ResetColorEnabled clears the override and reverts to TTY detection.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ResetColorEnabled() then format.ColorEnabled(pipe)\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true); format.ResetColorEnabled()\"\n    expected:\n      color_enabled_pipe: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.7\n\n  - name: color_enabled_pipe\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for an os.Pipe writer.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(pipeWriter)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: color_enabled_non_file\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for a bytes.Buffer (non-*os.File).\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(&bytes.Buffer{})\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: human_size_binary\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1024-based units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1536, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.5K\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n      - prd003-format R3.3\n\n  - name: human_size_si\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1000-based SI units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1000000, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.0MB\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n\n  - name: human_size_zero\n    description: HumanSize returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(0, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"0\"'\n    traces: